        "original_id": "61e2c842-5e1e-519d-9141-b0948de07cbc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jim Thorpe, Eddie Mahan\n- Organizations: Indians\n- Places: LaRue, Ohio\n- Topics: Native American athletes, football\n\nFacts:\n- The Indians were a team based in LaRue, Ohio, composed only of Native Americans, and Jim Thorpe coached the team.\n- Jim Thorpe was a member of the Sac and Fox Nation.\n- Jim Thorpe became the first Native American to win a gold medal for his home country.\n- Eddie Mahan was widely regarded as one of the greatest football players in the first 50 years of the sport.\n- Jim Thorpe named Eddie Mahan the greatest football player of all time.",
